// =====================================================================
// SCENE 5 · DAY 3: RETRACING THE DREAM (MIDPOINT)
// Anin follows her dream step by step and realizes her dream self has
// been killing Fal. She undoes the trap, moves the session back to the
// library, and saves him. No death, so a SOFT RESET at midnight.
//
// NOTES FOR THE PROGRAMMER
// - Every "//" comment is a stage direction for you, not in-game text.
// - Commands used (new ones marked NEW):
//     <<enable_control>>, <<quest_start>>, <<quest_update>>,
//     <<scene_transition>>, <<advance_time>>, <<event_marker>>,
//     <<npc_enter>>, <<npc_exit>>, <<remove_item>>  (same as before)
//     <<memory_montage true/false>> NEW  screen dims, gap colour grade
//                                    bleeds in at the edges
//     <<stay_awake "fail">>      NEW  screen slowly dims; Anin falls
//                                    asleep. (Scene 7 uses "success".)
//     <<soft_reset>>             NEW  midnight loop back to Dec 10, no
//                                    white flash
// - Speaker "Night Anin" = Anin's own voice from the gaps, played back
//   as memory. Same voice actor/text style as night Anin later.
// - Speaker "Note" = text shown on screen in Anin's handwriting.
// - World state at start: ROOFTOP KEY is in Anin's blazer (from Gap 2).
//   Flag in the auditorium is crooked; one flagpole screw is loose.
//   Fal has the auditorium note in his locker.
// =====================================================================


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — MORNING
// Same interactables as Day 2 (bed, poster, desk, Kirana's bed, door),
// plus Day3_Dorm_Blazer.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day3_Start
tags: scene5 day3 dorm
---
<<sfx "alarm_clock">>
// Lets the Dorm door run Day3_Dorm_Door instead of leaving freely.
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<set $d3_dressed to false>>
<<set $d3_found_key to false>>
<<set $d3_seen_flag to false>>
<<set $d3_seen_base to false>>
<<set $d3_undo_base to false>>
<<set $d3_undo_flag to false>>
// Kirana is still asleep.
Anin: Ugh, that dream again. What is it, anyway?
Anin: And why does Fal always die, even when I tried to stop it the night before?
<<enable_control>>
<<quest_start "day3" "Get ready for school">>
===

title: Day3_Dorm_Blazer
tags: scene5 day3 dorm interactable required
---
// Anin's blazer on the chair. NEW interactable today.
<<if $d3_found_key is false>>
    <<sfx "blazer_key">>
    Anin: There's something in the pocket.
    Anin: ...The rooftop key.
    Anin: "He won't go up there tonight." I said that. In the dream, I said that.
    Anin: I have to check.
    <<set $d3_found_key to true>>
    <<set $d3_dressed to true>>
    <<quest_start "day3_event" "What did I do last night?">>
<<else>>
    Anin: The key's still in my pocket.
<<endif>>
===

title: Day3_Dorm_Door
tags: scene5 day3 dorm interactable
---
<<if $d3_found_key is false>>
    Anin: Something feels off. I should look around first.
<<else>>
    Anin: Leave the room?
    -> Yes
        // The marker goes first: nothing after <<scene_transition>> runs.
        <<event_marker "day3_auditorium" true>>
        <<scene_transition "LockerRoom">>
    -> Later
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// EVENT: WHAT DID I DO LAST NIGHT?
// Trigger: enter the Auditorium. Packed with students (basketball,
// chilling in the shade).
// Interactables: Day3_Aud_Hoop, Day3_Aud_Stage, Day3_Aud_Flag,
// Day3_Aud_FlagpoleBase (enabled only after the flag).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day3_Auditorium
tags: scene5 day3 auditorium event
---
<<event_marker "day3_auditorium" false>>
<<sfx "basketball_practice">>
Anin: Everything looks the same as in my dream. Except for the people.
Anin: Now... what did I do last night?
===

title: Day3_Aud_Hoop
tags: scene5 day3 auditorium interactable
---
Anin: In the dream, it was so quiet in here.
===

title: Day3_Aud_Stage
tags: scene5 day3 auditorium interactable
---
Anin: Ready for tomorrow. Like it was last night.
===

title: Day3_Aud_Flag
tags: scene5 day3 auditorium interactable
---
<<if $d3_undo_base is true and $d3_undo_flag is false>>
    <<sfx "flag_cloth">>
    // Anin pulls the rope; the flag hangs straight.
    Anin: Straight. Nothing to fix.
    <<set $d3_undo_flag to true>>
    <<jump Day3_Undo_Check>>
<<elseif $d3_undo_flag is true>>
    Anin: Straight. Nothing to fix.
<<else>>
    <<sfx "flag_cloth">>
    Anin: It's crooked. Exactly like last night.
    Anin: "He'll want to fix it."
    Anin: ...Why would I say that?
    <<set $d3_seen_flag to true>>
    // Enable Day3_Aud_FlagpoleBase now.
<<endif>>
===

title: Day3_Aud_FlagpoleBase
tags: scene5 day3 auditorium interactable
---
<<if $d3_seen_flag is false>>
    // Should not be reachable; the base is hidden until the flag is examined.
<<elseif $d3_seen_base is false>>
    // Anin kneels. Nobody in the hall notices.
    Anin: One of the screws. It's loose.
    Anin: Loose by hand. Not by time.
    Anin: I was kneeling right here. My hands were—
    <<set $d3_seen_base to true>>
    <<jump Day3_Montage>>
<<elseif $d3_undo_base is false>>
    <<sfx "bolt_tighten">>
    Anin: Tight. As tight as it goes.
    <<set $d3_undo_base to true>>
    <<jump Day3_Undo_Check>>
<<else>>
    Anin: Tight. As tight as it goes.
<<endif>>
===

title: Day3_Montage
tags: scene5 day3 auditorium cutscene
---
<<memory_montage true>>
// Each line plays in night Anin's voice, the exact words from the gaps.
Night Anin: "If I understand him, I can end this."
Night Anin: "He has to read these. This time it'll work."
Night Anin: "He won't go up there tonight."
Night Anin: "He'll want to fix it."
Night Anin: "It's done."
// The blur from Gap 1 clears. For the first time the player sees what
// the notes said, in Anin's handwriting. TWO LINES ONLY. Don't linger.
Note: "You will never be enough."
Note: "You're a disgrace to your family."
// Anin's own line from Day 2, in her day voice.
Anin: "Someone who believes in you."
<<memory_montage false>>
// Back to the noisy auditorium.
Anin: That was me.
Anin: The notes. The key. The screw. I did all of it.
Anin: I've been killing him.
// MIDPOINT: Anin now believes she sleepwalks and that her dream self is
// a bad side of her. She does NOT know yet that it's another Anin.
Anin: ...Then I can undo it.
<<quest_update "day3_event" "Undo what I did">>
// Player must now use the flagpole base again, then the flag.
===

title: Day3_Undo_Check
tags: scene5 day3 auditorium
---
<<if $d3_undo_base and $d3_undo_flag>>
    <<quest_update "day3_event" "Meet Fal at the lockers. Keep him away from here">>
    <<advance_time "after_school">>
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOCKER ROOM — AFTER SCHOOL (required)
// Trigger: enter the Locker Room after the bell. Fal arrives on time.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day3_Lockers
tags: scene5 day3 lockers event
---
<<npc_enter "Fal">>
Fal: There you are. I almost went to the auditorium.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<move_character_to_actor "Fal" "Anin" -2.5 10 "walk">>
// He holds up the auditorium note from Gap 2.
Fal: You left this in my locker, right? Looks like your writing.
-> ...Let's go to the library. Like we planned.
-> I didn't write that. Not awake, anyway.
    Fal: What?
Anin: Nothing. Library. Come on.
<<scene_transition_at_x "Library" -0.7 "sit">>
<<jump Day3_Library>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LIBRARY — STUDY SESSION (required)
// Quiet table by the window. Late sunlight. The promise is kept.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day3_Library
tags: scene5 day3 library event
---
// Anin sits on the left chair; Fal is already seated on the right one (SitPose Start Sitting).
// The X here sets her seat, also when Play starts in the Library (Playtest Start skips the lockers transition).
<<teleport_character "Anin" -0.7 "sit">>
Fal: Okay. Integrals. Go easy on me.
-> You're better at this than you think.
-> Your dad's not here. It's just us.
Fal: ...You'd be the first person to say that.
Anin: What do you actually want to do? After all this.
Fal: Medicine. That's the plan.
Anin: I didn't ask about the plan.
// Long pause before the next line.
Fal: ...Rockets. Stupid, right?
Anin: Not stupid.
Fal: Hey. That thing I wanted to tell you.
Fal: Tomorrow. After graduation. I'll tell you then.
Anin: ...Tomorrow.
<<npc_exit "Fal">>
<<scene_transition "Dorm">>
<<jump Day3_Dorm_Evening>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — EVENING
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Day3_Dorm_Evening
tags: scene5 day3 dorm
---
// Anin on her bed, watching the window. The sky goes dark.
// No sound from above. No screams.
Anin: He's alive.
Anin: He's alive, because I was there this time.
Anin: So when I sleep... it's me.
<<door_enter "Kirana" "Dorm">>
// Kirana drops onto her bed.
<<sfx "bed_drop">>
Kirana: You look like you saw a ghost.
<<face_character "Anin" "right">>
-> Maybe I did.
-> Just tired.
Anin: I can't sleep tonight. I won't.
<<stay_awake "fail">>
<<set $chapter_scene to 6>>
<<soft_reset>>
// TRANSITION → Scene 6: Gap 3
===
